%U A397935 315392661183600,922690120934400,2498927260269440,6331024753095168,15131433870363024,34354020355545600,74518498900780200,155180855615052960,311515828067504984,604942108306728192
%N A397935 Number of n X n binary matrices with exactly 14 1's such that there are an even number of 1's in every row and column.
%C A397935 Weight A_14 of the weight distribution for a square n X n Single Parity Check Product Code (SPCP) code when the 1's represent bit errors, and 0's represent unchanged bits. For even parity SPCP code, A_odd = 0, A_4 = C(n,2)^2 = A000537(n-1), A_6 = 3!*C(n,3)^2 = A179058(n), A_8 = A396317(n), A_10 = A396321(n), A_12 = A393842(n). See the rectangular formula link for other message data formats.
%D A397935 E. R. Berlekamp, Algebraic Coding Theory, McGraw-Hill, New York, 1968, pp. 397-400.
%D A397935 R. E. Blahut, Theory and Practice of Error Control Codes, Addison-Wesley, 1983, p. 431.
%D A397935 C. Leung, Evaluation of the Error Probability of Single Parity-Check Codes, IEEE Transactions on Communications Vol. COM-31, NO. 2, Feb 1983, pp. 250-253.
%D A397935 F. J. MacWilliams and N. J. A. Sloane The Theory of Error Correcting Codes, Elsevier/North Holland 1977, p. 21.
%D A397935 W. W. Peterson and E. J. Weldon, Error Correcting Codes, MIT Press, 1994, pp. 64-70, pp. 131-132.
%H A397935 G. Gordon Thompson, <a href="/A397935/b397935.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..500</a>
%H A397935 A. M. Patel and S. J. Hong, <a href="/A397935/a397935.pdf">Optimal Rectangular Code for High Density Magnetic Tapes</a>
%H A397935 G. Gordon Thompson, <a href="/A397935/a397935.txt">Program For Coefficients of Subsets A_14 </a>
%H A397935 G. Gordon Thompson, <a href="/A397935/a397935.jpg">Diagram for Subsets 14 1's</a>
%H A397935 G. Gordon Thompson, <a href="/A396317/a396317_2.pdf">Probability of Undetected Error for Some Simple Product Codes</a>, MS Thesis, UT Arlington TX, May 1984, pp. 35-37.
%H A397935 G. Gordon Thompson, <a href="/A397935/a397935_1.txt">Rectangular formula for a(n,k)</a>
%H A397935 <a href="/index/Rec#order_15">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (15,-105,455,-1365,3003,-5005,6435,-6435,5005,-3003,1365,-455,105,-15,1).
%F A397935 a(n) = 3110940*C(n,7)^2 + 4233600*C(n,7)*C(n,6) + 911400*C(n,7)*C(n,5) + 65520*C(n,7)*C(n,4) + 1092*C(n,7)*C(n,3) + 1080000*C(n,6)^2 + 316800*C(n,6)*C(n,5) + 11520*C(n,6)*C(n,4) + 14600*C(n,5)^2 + 480*C(n,5)*C(n,4).
%F A397935 For rectangular formula for the n X k matrices, see link.
%F A397935 From _Jianing Song_, Jul 26 2026: (Start)
%F A397935 a(n) = n^2*(n - 1)^2*(n - 2)^2*(n - 3)*(n - 4)*(2469*n^6 - 48081*n^5 + 388163*n^4 - 1669899*n^3 + 4057216*n^2 - 5295788*n + 2906640)/20160.
%F A397935 G.f.: 8*x^5*(2125 + 433425*x + 13658670*x^2 + 117491822*x^3 + 372803886*x^4 + 490721070*x^5 + 273896945*x^6 + 61019745*x^7 + 4501428*x^8 + 64144*x^9)/(1 - x)^15.
%F A397935 E.g.f.: x^5*(2856000 + 101371200*x + 550482240*x^2 + 901667648*x^3 + 617389528*x^4 + 205590168*x^5 + 35624890*x^6 + 3237878*x^7 + 144501*x^8 + 2469*x^9)*exp(x)/20160. (End)
%e A397935 The first formula given above adds the counts of 10 subsets that are categorized by number of nonzero rows and columns (with transpositions in the same category).
%e A397935 For n=0 to 4, a(n)=0.
%e A397935 For n=5, a(5) = 3110940*0 + 4233600*0 + 911400*0 + 65520*0 + 1092*0 + 1080000*0 + 316800*0 + 11520*0 + 14600*1*1 + 480*1*5 = 17000.
%e A397935 For n=6, a(6) = 3110940*0 + 4233600*0 + 911400*0 + 65520*0 + 1092*0 + 1080000*1*1 + 316800*1*6 + 11520*1*15 + 14600*6*6 + 480*6*15 = 3722400.
%e A397935 For n=7, a(7) = 3110940*1*1 + 4233600*1*7 + 911400*1*21 + 65520*1*35 + 1092*1*35 + 1080000*7*7 + 316800*7*21 + 11520*7*35 + 14600*21*21 + 480*21*35 = 163320360.
%e A397935 See link for Diagram of Subsets for 14 1's. The coefficient 3110940 is for the case of two 1's in every column and row, no odd, see A001499(7).
%o A397935 (BASIC) 'For Coefficients of Formulas, not the sequence terms. See Link.
